\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The paper in one figure: the statistic moves, admission does not, suppression does not follow.} \textbf  {(a)} A preservation criterion reasons along one chain: statistic $\to $ decision $\to $ admitted adversarial contribution $\to $ suppression. \textbf  {The last two links are the ones we break}, each broken arrow annotated with the arm that witnesses it. The lower arc is why they must be broken by intervening rather than comparing, and \textbf  {Mode~S cuts it by construction}; \textbf  {the three annotations are three scopes, not one experiment} (App.~\ref {app:story}). \textbf  {(b)} Mode~S, Krum under model-scaling (§\ref {sec:targeted}): as $\rho $ grows to $54.6$ the \emph  {decision} flips in up to $80\%$ of rounds while the \emph  {support} of the admitted adversarial mass does not, and max-committed ASR stays inside the pre-registered $\pm 0.15$ practical-equivalence margin ($|\Delta |{=}0.026$). Error bars here are Student-$t$ $95\%$ intervals on the levels ($n{=}5$). \textbf  {(c)} \textbf  {Six cells, one contrast each, estimated two ways} (App.~\ref {app:sixcell}); each connector's length is how much the answer moves when the attenuation channel is closed. \textbf  {The two designs disagree on $4$ of $6$ cells, and on \texttt  {coord\_median}/pixel they have opposite signs}: $-0.272$ $[-0.422,-0.122]$ against $+0.098$ $[+0.018,+0.178]$, intervals excluding zero and not overlapping, so the confounded estimate is differently signed rather than noisier. Above the dashed rule are the four cells a pre-registered mechanism was read off, so they are \emph  {training data, not evidence for it}; below are its two out-of-sample cells. One confirms, \textbf  {one refutes, and we withdraw it} (§\ref {sec:targeted_rest}).}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:modeS}{{1}{2}{\textbf {The paper in one figure: the statistic moves, admission does not, suppression does not follow.} \textbf {(a)} A preservation criterion reasons along one chain: statistic $\to $ decision $\to $ admitted adversarial contribution $\to $ suppression. \textbf {The last two links are the ones we break}, each broken arrow annotated with the arm that witnesses it. The lower arc is why they must be broken by intervening rather than comparing, and \textbf {Mode~S cuts it by construction}; \textbf {the three annotations are three scopes, not one experiment} (App.~\ref {app:story}). \textbf {(b)} Mode~S, Krum under model-scaling (§\ref {sec:targeted}): as $\rho $ grows to $54.6$ the \emph {decision} flips in up to $80\%$ of rounds while the \emph {support} of the admitted adversarial mass does not, and max-committed ASR stays inside the pre-registered $\pm 0.15$ practical-equivalence margin ($|\Delta |{=}0.026$). Error bars here are Student-$t$ $95\%$ intervals on the levels ($n{=}5$). \textbf {(c)} \textbf {Six cells, one contrast each, estimated two ways} (App.~\ref {app:sixcell}); each connector's length is how much the answer moves when the attenuation channel is closed. \textbf {The two designs disagree on $4$ of $6$ cells, and on \texttt {coord\_median}/pixel they have opposite signs}: $-0.272$ $[-0.422,-0.122]$ against $+0.098$ $[+0.018,+0.178]$, intervals excluding zero and not overlapping, so the confounded estimate is differently signed rather than noisier. Above the dashed rule are the four cells a pre-registered mechanism was read off, so they are \emph {training data, not evidence for it}; below are its two out-of-sample cells. One confirms, \textbf {one refutes, and we withdraw it} (§\ref {sec:targeted_rest})}{figure.caption.1}{}}
